  "id": "KP280",
  "version": "2.0",
  "title": "Ankle replacement",
  "description": "An ankle replacement is an outpatient surgical procedure where your surgeon removes damaged bone surfaces from your ankle joint and replaces them with artificial components. Ankle replacement is performed when severe arthritis has damaged your ankle beyond repair. The procedure takes 1-2 hours, and you may go home the same day or stay overnight. You'll wear a cast or boot and use crutches for 4-6 weeks while you heal. Unlike ankle fusion, which locks the joint, ankle replacement preserves some motion. Physical therapy helps you restore strength and learn to use your new ankle. Full recovery typically takes 3-6 months. You may have some restrictions on high-impact activities like running, but you should be able to return to most normal activities. Your new ankle should provide pain relief and improved function compared to a damaged arthritic ankle.",
